# QUESTION: Does a managed device push metric samples to a real hub over TLS
# MuxConn, preserve its latest reading across disconnect while leaving an actual
# offline gap bucket in the series, record a fresh reading on reconnect, and
# retain both latest and series across a hub restart?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: sample interval negotiation, sample-report push, UTC slot
# ingestion, gap preservation, shutdown checkpoint flush, startup reload, and
# query execution run across the real ze hub daemon, its ZeFS store, and SSH CLI.
# VALIDATES: fleet-8 AC-1, AC-3, AC-4, AC-11, AC-12. The fixture checks an
# unreported device, sends measured figures (including explicit zero while
# omitting absent owners), disconnects across a full UTC minute, reconnects with
# updated readings, verifies the gap bucket in show fleet sample series, and
# restarts the hub to confirm persisted latest, series, and gap survive.
option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=240s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture managed/fleet-history-reconnect $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=240s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: fleet metric history retained across disconnect, showed offline gap, updated on reconnect, and persisted across hub restart
